cripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":527,"character":4},"end":{"line":532,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"movement","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Movement","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Triggers a named scripted move from a Cutscener in the scene \u2014 e.g. <<movement JoshHome>> walks whatever object/destination pair was named \"JoshHome\" in that Cutscener's Inspector list. Optional modifier words, in any order: freeze \u2014 the dialogue waits until the move actually finishes before showing the next line. Without it, the line advances immediately and the move plays out in the background. hold   \u2014 the sprite KEEPS the facing it already had for the whole move, instead of turning to follow the direction of travel. Use it with a <<face>> right before, when a character has to walk while still looking at someone: floating backwards, backing away, being pulled. flip   \u2014 invert the sprite once before setting off, then hold that. Legacy: it's a guess about which way the art currently points, so <<face>> plus hold is the version that's actually right every time. e.g. <<movement JoshHome freeze>>, <<movement HazeFloatDown hold freeze>>.","language":"csharp","async":true,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":548,"character":4},"end":{"line":571,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"movementName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier1","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier2","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier3","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"enable","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Enable","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Shows/hides a named object from a Cutscener in the scene \u2014 e.g. <<enable ElderAmos>> / <<disable ElderAmos>>, matching whatever name was given to that entry in the Cutscener's Objects list.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":576,"character":4},"end":{"line":580,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"disable","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Disable","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":582,"character":4},"end":{"line":586,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"placeat","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.PlaceAt","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"<<placeat TrueHaze HazeThree>> \u2014 puts the first object exactly where the second one is, matching its facing, instantly. Made for swapping a cutscene stand-in for the real object: place, disable the stand-in, enable the real one, and the handover is invisible instead of the replacement popping in somewhere else.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":592,"character":4},"end":{"line":596,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"referenceName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"face","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Face","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Forces a named object's facing outright, instead of whatever direction a <<movement>> happened to travel in. Two forms: <<face Josh left>>      \u2014 a fixed compass direction: left, right, up, down. <<face Josh HazeOne>>   \u2014 turn to look at ANOTHER registered object, wherever it currently is. Use the second form any time the player walked to the spot HIMSELF rather than being placed there by a <<movement>> \u2014 it is the only one that stays correct no matter which side he approached from. Both names must be registered in a Cutscener's Objects list (the same list <<enable>>/<<disable>> use); they may be in different Cutsceners.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":608,"character":4},"end":{"line":612,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"towards","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"add_objective","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.AddObjectiveCommand","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to add objective","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":338,"character":4},"end":{"line":350,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectiveName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"open_quest_log","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.OpenQuestLogCommand","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to open quest log","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":381,"character":4},"end":{"line":386,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"close_quest_log","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.CloseQuestLogCommand","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to close quest log","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":389,"character":4},"end":{"line":394,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"follow","definitionName":"global::NpcFollow.StartFollowing","fileName":"ecdd-adventure-game-2026\\Assets\\Scripts\\NPC\\NpcFollow.cs","documentation":"Yarn: <<follow Marcus>> \u20